{"chunk_id": "102710d768e8", "text": "Bhishma narrates the final ascent of Suka, the son of Vyasa, as he completes his yogic quest for liberation. Having realized the path of Emancipation, Suka enters profound meditation, transcends space, and travels through the sky with the brilliance of fire and the swiftness of thought. Celestial beings\u2014Rishis, Apsaras, Gandharvas, and gods\u2014watch in awe as nature itself honors him with flowers and reverence. Detached from all worldly ties, he asks the universe to answer his father if Vyasa calls after him. Casting off successively the qualities of tamas, rajas, and even sattva, Suka reaches the attributeless state of Brahman. Cosmic disturbances mark the moment of his transcendence, and with unstoppable force he even splits the joined peaks of Meru and Himavat, symbolizing the soul\u2019s passage beyond all barriers into ultimate liberation.\nSuka attains complete detachment, ascends through the cosmos, and dissolves into attribute-less Brahman amid cosmic wonders and universal reverence.\nThemes: liberation (moksha), yogic transcendence, cosmic recognition, detachment from gunas, union with Brahman", "vector": [0.020128943026065826, -0.011068896390497684, 0.013900160789489746, -0.029687831178307533, -0.03723787143826485, 0.038343410938978195, -0.020075013861060143, -0.021841183304786682, -0.024969056248664856, -0.01586856320500374, 0.008621874265372753, 0.005332214757800102, 0.009504959918558598, 0.016057314351201057, 0.010098177008330822, -0.010677912272512913, 0.04379022493958473, -0.012680020183324814, -0.0072264657355844975, -0.0245241429656744, 0.001437540864571929, 0.0046243988908827305, 0.012862030416727066, 0.011682337149977684, -0.022555740550160408, 0.016475263983011246, 0.026735225692391396, -0.022380471229553223, -0.0003768699534703046, -0.005955767352133989, 0.0031362995505332947, 0.007084902375936508, -0.0090330820530653, -0.000823257549200207, -0.03402910381555557, -0.005625452846288681, -0.005308621097